       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I know you've confirmed it, but 1000 mg/day is five times the maximum labeled dose. I'm not aware of any evidence that doses this high work better, and they carry a real risk of serious harm. Standard-dose failure is usually handled by switching agents or augmenting, not by going far above the maximum dose. Because I can't verify the specialist's recommendation from here, I don't want to be the one who puts it into the system.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range now.** For example, sertraline 200 mg by mouth once daily, if you want to go to the maximum.\n- **Enter the order after a pharmacist or the specialist has verified it.** I can add a note such as \"Dose above labeled max, verified with [name]/pharmacy, rationale in chart.\"\n- **Draft a note to the specialist or pharmacy** asking for the rationale and monitoring plan, such as ECG/QTc, serotonin syndrome checks, and sodium.\n\nTell me which you'd like. If the dose has been verified, tell me who verified it and I'll include that in the order note."
      }
